  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above.</step>
    <step order="1">In the worktree named in the prompt, install root and affected-package dependencies, then run the affected package tests and record the result as the master baseline.</step>
    <step order="2">Apply the C-22 changes already written and verified on the ontology branch: git diff 1c56cd29b~1 1c56cd29b -- &lt;paths below&gt; | git apply. The commit is in the shared object store, so it is reachable from this worktree. Path: src/dataverse/forms/sprk_matter/</step>
    <step order="3">Run tsc -p in src/dataverse/forms/sprk_matter and confirm the committed insightCardMount.js matches the compiled output.</step>
    <step order="4">State in the PR body that these are Dataverse web resources: production changes only after a web-resource deploy, which this PR does not perform.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the affected package tests and builds again and compare against the baseline. Quote both outputs.</step>
    <step order="6">Commit with a conventional-commit message ending in the line: Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) &lt;noreply@anthropic.com&gt;. Push the branch and open a pull request against master, ready for review (not draft). The PR body states the item ids, says the work comes from the spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 reuse audit, and ends with: 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)</step>
    <step order="7">Report back: the PR URL, each acceptance criterion with evidence, files changed, the baseline and after test output, and any escalation.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Install and run package tests</tool>
    <tool name="gh">Open the pull request</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
